{ instr_mnemonic.init - a DSEE derived object of be_com/opcodes.def
  (cc.a88k only), which the opcode generator made with
  opcode_enumeration.ins.pas: the initializer of the section
  instruction_mnemonic (0x2B7A3C: 384 entries of 12 characters, the
  opcodes' names without the OPC$ prefix, "********" for 0).  Included
  by lst.pas after the opcode enumeration.

  No Apollo copy survives.  backend.ins.pas declares the section's
  variable (instruction_mnemonic) for every unit, so this file cannot
  declare it again with the initializer (dpc: already declared); the
  data are the opcode enumeration's identifiers
  (`tools/cc_enumnames.py ctape/.../cc.a88k 0x209FEE').

  Not known from the original: how Apollo's units shared the section
  (docs/questions.md, translator PB). }

{ TODO(pascal) instr_mnemonic.init: the section's initializer (see
  above) }
